/> man pwd

NAME
    pwd - print the working directory

SYNOPSIS
    pwd

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the absolute path of the current directory (the one the
    prompt shows), from the OS's GETCWD syscall. pwd is /BIN/PWD.

    The shell also has a built-in pwd, used only when /BIN/PWD is
    missing; it prints the same path.

LIMITS
    The OS keeps the path in 64 bytes.

EXAMPLES
    pwd              e.g.  /BIN

NOTES
    Ported from P8X os/commands/pwd.c 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
--More--            cd, dir, ls
